Which type of relationship does this graph show?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=6cm,height=5.5cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-4,xmax=4,ymin=-3,ymax=8,xtick={-4,-3,...,4},ytick={-2,0,...,8},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$}]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,<->,domain=-3:3,samples=100] {x*x-2};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which type of relationship does this graph show?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=6cm,height=5.5cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-3.3,xmax=3.3,ymin=-1,ymax=9,xtick={-3,-2,...,3},ytick={0,2,...,8},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$}]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,<->,domain=-3.3:3.17,samples=100] {exp(x*ln(2))};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which type of relationship does this graph show?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=6cm,height=5.5cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-4,xmax=4,ymin=-4,ymax=6,xtick={-4,-3,...,4},ytick={-4,-2,...,6},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$}]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,<->,domain=-4:4,samples=2] {x+1};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
